# IMAGE-LOSS-COPY-FX: a session whose first prompt carried image #1, kept as a
# blob (fx) or a copy (xfx) that is not there, resumed by id at launch. fx's
# reader refuses it, InvalidSessionFormat (decodeUser,
# session_adapter.zig:2871-2893@481104fd): its launch takes the terminal, gives
# it back, and says the session is unreadable (app_entry_runtime.zig:278-285);
# xfx says so before it takes the terminal. Neither touches the session
# (`home after`). `quit` is the first launch's exit, where the refusal's row
# starts. The seeds: fx's p5-effort-fork-v2 source with the image in its first
# prompt (receipts/image-loss-copy-fx/seed_fx.py) and the lock files fx keeps
# beside a session; xfx's written by its own store with the same id, workspace
# and image. p5-image-loss-whole is the same with the copy there: it resumes.
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0 FX_SESSIONS_V2=1
fx: homefile .fx/sessions/v2/index.jsonl p5-effort-fork-v2-index.jsonl
fx: homefile .fx/sessions/v2/index.lock p5-lifecycle-v1-plain-session.lock
fx: homefile .fx/sessions/v2/kH1xJ5Cm-oRk/log.jsonl p5-image-loss-gone-fx.jsonl
fx: homefile .fx/sessions/v2/kH1xJ5Cm-oRk/lock p5-lifecycle-v1-plain-session.lock
xfx: homefile .xfx/sessions/kH1xJ5Cm-oRk/events.jsonl p5-image-loss-gone-xfx-events.jsonl
xfx: homefile .xfx/sessions/kH1xJ5Cm-oRk/session.json p5-image-loss-gone-xfx-session.json
wait 3
keep
type /quit
key Enter
wait 2
snapfull quit
cursor quit
relaunch --resume kH1xJ5Cm-oRk
wait 4
snapfull refused
home after
